  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#6157\", \"PowerToys#22756\", \"PowerToys#150\"], \"answer\": \"PowerToys doesn't have this feature yet, and it has been requested many times before. Most of the other requests were closed as duplicates of PowerToys#6157 (folder and file color coding), which in turn was marked as a duplicate of the file tagging and color-coding request in PowerToys#150. Follow and upvote PowerToys#150 (or #6157) rather than filing a new request. You can add your use case there: you want a native option that replaces third-party colorizer apps that slow the system down. Until it exists, the threads suggest third-party tools such as Folder Marker or the Files app. One suggested approach is to recolor the folder icon with SHGetSetFolderCustomSettings, which stores the setting in desktop.ini.\"}",
